W44-207 — W44-94 OUTER `find_best_32x32_transform` widening with per-m3 sub-discriminator
========================================================================================

Status: HONEST-STOP (Phase 1 read-only analysis; no source change)
Parent commit: 49763e26 (W44-206 ruled out savings_factor recalibration)
Chunk source: W44-204 attack ranking, C3 pick (MED EV, MED confidence, 2.5d budget)
Predecessor: W44-167 (`1d317623`) honest-stop on INNER variant Z layer

Hypothesis (from W44-204 C3 ranking)
-------------------------------------

W44-94 honest-stopped on a wider `EntropyMulTable::high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed()`
OUTER table lift because 1531677 regressed SSIM2 by -0.30 to -0.74 under any
`dct16x32 >= 1.30`. W44-167 ported the W44-98/99 m3 sub-discriminator pattern to
the INNER variant Z layer and HONEST-STOPPED on three failure modes (1420710 d=5
SSIM2 -0.20 mean, 1531677 d=5 catastrophic Mode B, 1418519 d=6 W44-166 destruction).

C3 proposed re-applying the W44-94 mechanism at the OUTER layer (not INNER) with
a per-m3 sub-discriminator: `dct32x32 = 1.27` for high-m3 OUTER-firing images,
`dct32x32 = 1.34` (default) for low-m3.

Findings (Phase 1, read-only)
------------------------------

Three independent facts falsify the C3 hypothesis on current main:

**1. The cluster-#3 cells fire variant Z, NOT OUTER.**

The W44-94 honest-stop targeted {1420710, 1531677} on the OUTER table. Since
W44-96 (`f4ffbb2b`), both images pass the W44-96 variant Z gate
(`edge_density>=0.7 AND fcbr<0.01`) at d>=4.5. The W44-148/154/156/166 chain
already handles them on the INNER variant Z chain (HC for 1420710 m3=32.93,
LC for 1531677 m3=12.30, with d_high split at d>5.5). The OUTER table never
fires for them.

**2. The OUTER-only REJECT_Z images have ZERO zenjxl losers at d>=3.**

Of the 5 CID22 photos that pass the W44-29 OUTER gate (mask<50, d>=3):
- {1420710, 1531677}: routed to variant Z (item 1)
- {2389166, 1044329, 7062219}: REJECT_Z, get the default OUTER table

Per `benchmarks/w44_202_vs_w44_185.per_cell_diff.tsv`, the REJECT_Z images
have ZERO zenjxl cells with `delta_bytes_pct_new > 3.0` at d>=3:
- 2389166: 0 losers
- 1044329: 0 losers
- 7062219: 0 losers (only 2 cells at d=2.75 which is BELOW the OUTER gate)

W44-205 (`8fe99fb5`) already harvested -1.5% to -2.4% bytes on 7062219 e7
d=3/4/5 via the coeff_orders bucket-skip extension. The OUTER mechanism has
no remaining wins to harvest.

**3. The cells C3 INTENDED to close are SSIM2-axis losers, not bytes-axis.**

Per W44-202 (commit `5f3f5ca7`), 1420710 + 1531677 on zenjxl at d ∈ [3.0, 4.5)
(where OUTER would fire if variant Z gate failed) are:
- bytes_delta_pct_new: -1.9% to -7.6% (we WIN bytes vs cjxl)
- ssim2_delta_new:     -0.57 to -1.33 (we LOSE SSIM2 vs cjxl)

Wider OUTER lift would push the cost model FURTHER toward bytes-saving at the
expense of SSIM2. The W44-94 mechanism (`dct32x32=1.27` or `1.20`) makes
DCT32X32 cheaper relative to smaller blocks, encouraging larger-block selection
→ fewer coefficients → fewer bytes BUT lower fidelity. The cells need the
OPPOSITE direction (softer lift, more DCT16/DCT8).

**4. W44-167 already tested the per-m3 split mechanism.**

The W44-167 HONEST-STOP (Mode D = per-m3 split with HC->1.40, LC->1.26, Z->1.22)
falsified the m3 split as a load-bearing axis: 1420710 (HC, m3=32.93) and
1531677 (LC, m3=12.30) BOTH regressed under their respective Mode D lifts at
the INNER layer. The C3 chunk proposes the same split mechanism at OUTER —
but the only LOW-m3 image that fires OUTER (without variant Z) would be a
new corpus entrant; current OUTER-firing REJECT_Z images all sit at m3 ∈
[47.996, 65.031] (well above any m3 threshold we'd set).

In other words: there is no LOW-m3 REJECT_Z image in current corpus to PROTECT
from the lift. A per-m3 split has nothing to gate.

Honest-stop decision
---------------------

Per the W44-207 chunk spec (lines 47-49):
> Honest-stop conditions:
> - If m3 threshold can't cleanly split (e.g., 2389166 m3 falls in the regression zone): honest-stop, document
> - If wider lift introduces unforeseen regressions elsewhere: revert

All three OUTER REJECT_Z images sit at m3 >= 47.996 — there is no clean split
to make, only a uniform lift that has no measurable target cell to close AND
risks SSIM2 regression on the implicitly-targeted variant-Z cells (which fire
a different table layer entirely).

Per W44-204 ranking explicit DO NOT directives:
> 6. DO NOT respawn W44-93 / W44-94 / W44-150 / W44-165 / W44-167 / W44-198 /
>    W44-199 as the SAME chunk. C3 explicitly proposes a NEW mechanism layer
>    (OUTER not INNER) for the W44-94 wedge.

The W44-207 measurement confirms the new mechanism layer (OUTER) does NOT
have the target cells that motivated the C3 ranking. The audit conflated
W44-94's HISTORICAL target {1420710, 1531677} (which fired OUTER pre-W44-96)
with current state (where those images fire variant Z).

