Acceptance gates
----------------

The C3 chunk spec acceptance gates (Phase 2/3):
- (a) Build PASS — `cargo check` passes on parent commit (49763e26) with no
  changes. PASS.
- (b) Tests pass (1449+) — no code change, no test impact.
- (c) Hash-locks 36/36 Zenjxl BYTE-IDENTICAL — no source change.
- (d) Libjxl byte-lock BYTE-IDENTICAL — no source change.
- (e) divergence_table_drift 7/7 PASS — table entry note updated.
- (f) ≥6 of the 13 OPEN cells close — NOT MET because the cells aren't
  routed through OUTER; the mechanism is at the wrong layer.
- (g) 1531677 byte-identical — N/A (no source change).
- (h) Multi-decoder PASS on 3 spot cells — N/A (no source change).

Gates (a)-(e) trivially pass via no-source-change; (f) cannot be met by the
proposed mechanism. HONEST-STOP per task spec.

DO NOT (binding for future agents)
-----------------------------------

1. **DO NOT respawn C3 against a different cell subset.** Measurement shows
   no OUTER-only cell wants the lift, and no variant-Z cell can be helped
   by an OUTER-layer change (the variant Z routing pre-empts OUTER on the
   target images).

2. **DO NOT lower the W44-29 gate's `HIGH_D_PHOTO_SMOOTH_THRESHOLD = 50`** to
   pull more images into OUTER. The W44-151 honest-stop (`ef35c5e1`) already
   measured admit-by-mask_p25 on the OUTER table and found d=6 over-fires;
   the W44-152 narrow [3.0, 5.0] band IS the surgical fix.

3. **DO NOT raise the OUTER `dct32x32 = 1.34` to 1.27 or lower without a
   discriminator**. The W44-94 sweep on 1044329 e5 d=5 (the only REJECT_Z
   cell measured) showed Z (1.20) saves -1.92% bytes BUT the cell is already
   FIXED — the saved bytes don't move the ledger and risk untested SSIM2
   collateral on the other 2 REJECT_Z images.

4. **DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the residual cluster** (per W44-66 user
   correction).

5. **DO NOT spawn another OUTER-table chunk targeting cluster #3
   (1420710/1531677)**. Those cells fire variant Z; OUTER cannot affect
   them. W44-167 already tested the per-m3 split at variant Z (RULED OUT
   on three failure modes).

6. **DO NOT re-attempt the W44-94 widening at any layer without first
   addressing the buttloop measurement divergence** (W44-167 follow-on #5).

Follow-on candidates (NOT in W44-207 scope)
--------------------------------------------

1. **W44-168+ distance-narrowed Mode D on LC** — W44-167 surprise positive
   (1531677 d=6 +0.58 SSIM2) is the next-cleanest 1-cell win. Already
   queued in W44-167 follow-on list; needs a sub-d-band gate.

2. **3637739-class root cause re-investigation** — W44-198/199/200 all
   honest-stopped. Cluster #1 (132 cells, 100K bytes) is the highest-EV
   surface remaining but needs a multi-week fresh hypothesis set; not a
   ranked chunk per W44-204.

3. **Root-cause buttloop measurement divergence** — W44-167 follow-on #5,
   highest long-term EV, multi-week cross-crate work.

